Skales End User Licence Agreement

Version 1.3, 9 November 2026
The version you accept governs the Software supplied under it. The full text is shown before acceptance, can be saved, and is published with all earlier versions at https://skales.app/licence. For business customers the English text governs. If you are a consumer, the full text in the language you selected at acceptance forms part of the agreement, and any discrepancy with the English text is resolved in your favour.
Licensor: Skales ("Skales", "we"). Name and contact details are in section 12.
Software: Skales Desktop, Skales Mobile, Skales Code, Skales Relay client components and every update we provide (the "Software")

1. What this is
The Software is proprietary. It is licensed, not sold. It is not open source and it is not source-available. No source code is provided or promised under this agreement.

2. What you may do
2.1 Personal and educational use. If you are a private individual, a student, a teacher, or an educational institution, you may install and use the Software free of charge on devices you control. Educational use includes teaching, learning, and academic research by students and teachers and within non-commercial educational institutions, including public schools and universities. Payment of salaries to teaching staff does not by itself make such use commercial. This permission takes precedence over section 2.4.
2.2 Freelancers and small businesses. If you work as a freelancer, are self-employed, or run a business, and no more than two (2) people work in or for that business, you may install and use the Software free of charge for that business on devices you control, including commercially and for work you do for your clients. Everyone who works in or for the business counts: owners, partners, managing directors, employees, including part-time staff, and freelancers who work for the business on a regular basis. Subcontractors engaged for a single project do not count. A business that is controlled by, or part of, a larger organisation is counted together with that organisation. Under this permission:
(a) you may build, adapt, and use your own workflows, plugins, skills, and automations for your own business;
(b) the results and outputs you create with the Software are yours, and you may deliver them to your clients and charge for your work;
(c) handing your own workflows, plugins, skills, or automations for the Software to a client, or setting them up for or with a client, requires prior written permission from Skales; an email from Skales is sufficient;
(d) white-labelling, reselling, or sublicensing the Software, or the plugins, skills, and other extensions Skales supplies, is not covered by this permission and requires a separate written agreement (section 3.2).
Your clients need their own licence under this agreement to install or use the Software themselves. If your business grows to more than two people, you may continue under this permission for thirty (30) days; after that, continued use requires a written commercial licence. This permission takes precedence over section 2.4.
2.3 Evaluation. Any other organisation may install the Software to evaluate it for thirty (30) days, starting with the organisation's first use for evaluation, once per organisation. The evaluation never converts into a paid licence by itself.
2.4 Commercial use. Any other use by or for a company, a business, or a public body, or in exchange for money or other consideration, requires a written commercial licence from Skales. Contact: request@skales.app.

3. What you may not do
3.0 Your statutory rights. The restrictions in this section do not limit rights you cannot waive under applicable law. These include making a necessary backup copy; observing, studying, or testing the Software during authorised use; reproduction and adaptation necessary for its intended use, including error correction; and decompilation necessary to achieve interoperability of an independently created program, subject to the statutory conditions. They also do not restrict transfers protected by applicable exhaustion rules or rights granted under third-party component licences (section 6). Activities otherwise restricted by this section may be authorised in a separate written agreement with Skales.
3.1 You may not offer the Software, or any service built on it, to third parties as a hosted, managed, or software-as-a-service offering.
3.2 You may not rebrand, white-label, resell, sublicense, rent, lease, or redistribute the Software, in whole or in part, including the plugins, skills, and other extensions Skales supplies with or for it, except as section 3.0 permits.
3.3 You may not reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or extract the Software, or otherwise attempt to derive its source code, models, prompts, or internal structure, except as section 3.0 permits.
3.4 You may not remove, hide, or alter any licence, trademark, attribution, or origin marking in the Software or its packages. Platform functions that an app store is required to permit, such as icon theming or family sharing, are not affected.
3.5 You may not copy or incorporate Skales' protected code, texts, prompts, tool definitions, or assets into another product without our written permission. This does not prohibit independent development that uses unprotected ideas, functionality, or interfaces, and it does not restrict the rights in section 3.0. Skales claims no ownership of your inputs or of the outputs you create with the Software.
3.6 You must install and run the Software as published. You may not modify the Software, remove or bypass its integrity, attestation, licence, or authentication mechanisms, or distribute or run a modified copy, except for adaptations section 3.0 permits.
3.7 You may not operate the Software commercially as a component, backend, agent engine, or library of another product or service, and you may not connect a third-party client to its relay or online services or collect its output in bulk, including for training models. Using the Software's own tools and interfaces on your own devices, including starting it from scripts, development environments, or assistive tools, remains free.
3.8 You may install official, unmodified packages through distribution channels authorised by Skales, including direct downloads where we offer them. You may not distribute re-signed or modified packages, bundle the Software, broker access to it, or submit it to any app store or distribution channel without our written permission. Managed distribution within an organisation requires a commercial licence.
3.9 You may not present yourself as a partner, reseller, certified provider, co-developer, or spokesperson of Skales or Mario Simic, falsely claim that Skales is part of, based on, or endorses another product, or use the name, likeness, or statements of Mario Simic in advertising. Factual statements that your setup runs, installs, or interoperates with Skales, editorial reporting, quotations permitted by law, and factual product comparisons remain unaffected.

4. Your data and your keys
The Software runs on your own devices. Provider keys, conversations, files, and memory stay on your devices unless you connect a service yourself. When you use optional online services, the Software exchanges the data those services need, such as licence and update checks, relay messages and their delivery metadata, and reports you choose to send. Skales IQ, Skales Relay, and other optional online services have their own terms, shown before you enable them. Information about personal data processed by Skales, including purposes, legal bases, recipients, retention periods, and your rights, is available in our Privacy Notice at https://skales.app/privacy, before acceptance and within the Software. Accepting this agreement is not consent to optional personal-data processing.

5. Trademarks
"Skales", the Skales logo, and the names of Skales products are trademarks of Mario Simic. This agreement grants no trademark rights. The trademark guidelines are included with the Software as TRADEMARK.md and published at https://skales.app/licence.

6. Third-party components
The Software contains open-source components under their own licences, listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, which is included with the Software and published at https://skales.app/licence. Those licences govern those components and grant you the rights they state; they do not extend to the Software as a whole.

7. Updates, term, and termination
7.1 We provide updates required by applicable law, including security updates for the period the law requires. Additional features or upgrades are included only where expressly agreed. Consumers are informed of updates within the Software.
7.2 The licence continues unless terminated in accordance with this section. We may terminate it by notice identifying a material breach. If the breach can be remedied, we allow a reasonable period of at least fourteen (14) days to remedy it before termination takes effect. Immediate termination is permitted only where the circumstances justify termination for cause without a remedy period. You may terminate at any time by deleting the Software.
7.3 After termination you must stop using and delete the proprietary Software. You need not delete your own data or independently licensed third-party components. Termination does not remove accrued claims, your right to retrieve your data, or rights you already hold under an earlier version of this agreement for the Software supplied under it.
7.4 This agreement does not authorise public identification of users or publication of alleged breaches. Statutory rights to enforce claims and to make lawful disclosures remain unaffected.
7.5 Sections 3.4, 3.5, 5, 6, 8, and 9 continue to apply to copies you obtained under this agreement after termination.

8. Warranty and liability
8.1 If you are a consumer, statutory liability and your statutory rights concerning the supply and conformity of the Software apply without contractual limitation. These include applicable rights to remedies for defects and to necessary updates. We do not provide any additional voluntary guarantee.
8.2 Nothing in this agreement excludes or limits liability for death or personal injury, for intentional misconduct or gross negligence, or any liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, including applicable product liability.
8.3 For business customers, the Software is provided "as is", and liability for slight negligence, indirect or consequential damages, loss of data, and loss of profit is excluded to the extent permitted by law. Different liability provisions may be agreed in the commercial licence.

9. Governing law
Austrian law applies. If you are a consumer, this choice does not deprive you of the protection of mandatory provisions of the law of your habitual residence that would apply without this choice. Consumers retain all statutory rights concerning jurisdiction. For business customers, the courts having subject-matter jurisdiction in Vienna, Austria, have exclusive jurisdiction.

10. Entire agreement
This agreement, together with the documents it names, is the complete licence for the Software supplied under it. Individually agreed terms and a separate commercial licence prevail over conflicting provisions of this agreement. Publishing revised terms does not by itself amend an existing agreement; a new version applies only to the Software you accept it for. Refusing revised terms does not terminate rights already granted under an earlier version for the Software supplied under it. If any provision is invalid, the remaining provisions remain in force.

